`@PACKAGE_NAME@` is a standalone Mojo library backed by Rust's `@RUST_CRATE@`
`@RUST_VERSION@`. The initial repository shell proves ordinary Mojo imports;
the completed binding must replace that proof with its reviewed public API,
representative examples, and documented semantic limits.

@README_GIT_INSTALL@

## Development

```sh
pixi install
pixi run t
pixi run examples
pixi run check-generated
```

Build the root Mojo package and generated Rust-binding source package together:

```sh
pixi publish --target-dir ./artifacts
```

## Provenance

The binding is generated from exact Rust source by
[`bind-rust-to-mojo`](@SKILL_REPOSITORY@/blob/main/SKILL.md). Generated ABI and
wrapper files are checked against their committed manifests; they are evidence
for this crate, not templates for another binding.
